[32]
Town square (on the bicycle)
Altenkirchen is a small town that mostly consists of two-storey houses, rather
small dwellings, but you also see a few public buildings among them, like a book
store to the south, a cemetery behind a fence to the north and an old candy shop
to the northwest, opposite to a church to the southeast.

You get off the bicycle.

> nw

In front of the shop
The old candy shop is located in a side alley of the town, probably the oldest
part of Altenkirchen. The shop is a flat-roofed grey building that surely has
seen better times than these. The paint was washed away from the facade exposing
it shelterless to wind and weather. There's a sign over the closed door to the
north, opposite to an old factory to the south, and you can see the town square
to the southeast.

Streams of water are running across the ground.

> s

Old factory
You are quite surprised that this building is crumbled down to its foundations.
The only thing which is still intact is the facade to the street, while the
remains of the building are just rests of walls, covered by dense undergrowth.
The only way back is north.

> remove undergrowth
You yank at the undergrowth and suddenly a whole part of it gives in, revealing
an old shelf and a counter.

> get shelf
You can't take the shelf.

> get tin
You take the tin off the shelf.

> open tin
You open the tin, revealing some oil.

> fill tin in lamp
You fill the content of the tin into the lamp and dispose it.

A torrent of water hits you directly into your face.

> find bike
(attempting to go to the town square)
(attempting to go north)

In front of the shop
The old candy shop is located in a side alley of the town, probably the oldest
part of Altenkirchen. The shop is a flat-roofed grey building that surely has
